# Every gene adds one row to each of these two files, at a shared per-letter
# anchor, so two gene PRs collide on the same line even though both rows belong.
# Replayed over the last 60 merges of each file, 34 of 118 consecutive pairs
# collided, and keeping both sides gave every row exactly once in a file that
# parses. Anything union gets wrong is caught later: a twice-edited row fails
# `test_genes`, and a broken file fails to compile.
#
# Do not add a file here unless its conflicts are appends of independent lines.
src/ai/advanced/genes.rs merge=union
src/ai/advanced/treatment_flags.rs merge=union
